# Verifying Clavyn UI changes

After making changes to the Clavyn frontend, verify behavior with the
composable CLI at `scripts/verify/control-clavyn.mjs`. It drives the live
renderer over CDP (via Playwright) with a persistent harness server, so
state survives across commands.

## Prerequisites (once per machine)

```bash
cd desktop && npm install
cd desktop/e2e && npm install && npx playwright install chromium
cd desktop && npm run dev   # Vite dev server on :1420
```

## Workflow

1. `node scripts/verify/control-clavyn.mjs doctor --pretty` — check environment
2. `node scripts/verify/control-clavyn.mjs home` / `navigate <view>` — navigate
3. `node scripts/verify/control-clavyn.mjs snapshot --pretty` — a11y tree
4. `node scripts/verify/control-clavyn.mjs click --name "text"` / `type` / `press` — interact
5. `node scripts/verify/control-clavyn.mjs screenshot /tmp/proof.png` — evidence
6. `node scripts/verify/control-clavyn.mjs console --pretty` — must be clean (no errors)
7. `node scripts/verify/control-clavyn.mjs stop` — tear down when done

## Feature Map

Read `scripts/verify/features/README.md` before navigating — it catalogs
every view, what it does, how to reach it, and the exact CLI commands.

## Rules

- Never assert "it works" without a `snapshot`/`screenshot` and a clean
  `console` as evidence.
- The fixture mocks SSH/SFTP/vault — this verifies the **renderer**, not
  end-to-end SSH. Core Rust logic is verified with `cargo test -p clavyn-core`.
- Destructive commands accept `--dry-run`.
- Full docs: `scripts/verify/README.md`. Help: `node scripts/verify/control-clavyn.mjs help`.
